2026-08-22T00:06Z  By-hand derivation of the eps^2 matching (recorded here before coding):
  g_r(m-1,b) = F + eps(G-F') + eps^2(H-G'+F''/2) + O(eps^3)
  m[g_r(m)-g_r(m-1)] = tF' + eps*t(G'-F''/2) + eps^2*t(H'-G''/2+F'''/6) + O(eps^3)
  h_{r-1}(n-m+1,b) at s=(1-t)+eps:
     Hhat_{r-1} + eps[Hhat'_{r-1}+K_{r-1}] + eps^2[Hhat''_{r-1}/2+K'_{r-1}+L_{r-1}] + O(eps^3)
  => eps^0 = Fact 2 (checks), eps^1 = Fact 3 (checks -- rearranges exactly to the
     documented G_r ODE, so the derivation scheme is validated one order down), and
  => H_r ODE:  t H_r' + (1+r+b) H_r
        = r[ Hhat''_{r-1}(1-t,b)/2 + K'_{r-1}(1-t,b) + L_{r-1}(1-t,b) ]
          + (t/2)G_r'' - (t/6)F_r''' + (1+r+b)[ G_r' - F_r''/2 ]
  => L_r relation (eps^2 of the source step, no ODE):
        L_r(s,b) = r K_{r-1}(s,b+1) + (1-s) H_r(1-s,b+1) - (1+b+r) G_r(1-s,b+1)
  Base: H_0==0, L_0==0 (exact, from g_0=1/(b+1) and h_0=(n-a+1)/(n(b+2))).

